WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.771
c. AD 220 · Llandough hill, above the
River Ely

2
00:00:03.811 --> 00:00:08.560
Spoken in Welsh, the living descendant of
the Brittonic they spoke

3
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:16.300
The stone house built here in the 2nd
century is being enlarged

4
00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:23.190
[in Welsh] One more course before the
rain, and the new room has its walls.

5
00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:26.380
The lime is good; it will set like rock.

6
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.089
[in Welsh] Make it wide. My father built
for one hearth.

7
00:00:31.129 --> 00:00:34.850
I want room for the winter, and room for
the grain.

8
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.176
[in Welsh] The barley's in and the spelt
is dry.

9
00:00:45.216 --> 00:00:48.727
The buyer for the fort will come before
the new moon.

10
00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:54.746
[in Welsh] Then there'll be silver for the
roof tiles. But keep back the best seed.

11
00:00:54.786 --> 00:00:56.441
Don't let him take it all.

12
00:01:03.584 --> 00:01:07.640
[in Welsh] Your mother lived all her life
in a round house.

13
00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.042
She'd laugh to see walls of stone and a
red roof.

14
00:01:11.668 --> 00:01:17.924
[in Welsh] Let her laugh. Stone stands.
Our grandchildren will sit at this hearth.

